        {
          "doc": "`set_recovery_escrow` was given an address that does not point back at a RecoveryEscrow\\nconfigured for this same underlying -- most likely a stale address copied from a\\ndifferent market. Found during audit review: this wiring is one-shot and irreversible,\\nso an admin mistake here previously had no cross-check at all, unlike `initialize`.",
          "name": "RecoveryEscrowMismatch",
          "value": 14
        },
        {
          "doc": "A fixed-point intermediate (balance, total supply, or allowance) overflowed/underflowed\\n`i128`. Found during an audit review: every balance/supply/allowance update here used raw\\n`+`/`-`, relying entirely on the workspace's `overflow-checks = true` release-profile\\nsetting to fail closed, as a generic Rust panic rather than this contract's own\\nobservable error code -- inconsistent with how `YTToken`/`PrincipalManager` already\\nharden their own arithmetic (`mul_div`/`ceil_mul_div`, per their own doc comments citing\\na prior audit finding).",
          "name": "ArithmeticOverflow",
          "value": 15
        }
      ]
